247
00:16:34,113 --> 00:16:37,525
Once its underside's exposed,
we may be able to attack it.

248
00:16:46,673 --> 00:16:50,233
You're pretty fast there,
Jojirou, but not too bright.

249
00:16:52,033 --> 00:16:54,739
Your body's reeking, you
haven't even noticed.

250
00:16:55,093 --> 00:16:56,453
Try paying attention.

251
00:16:58,313 --> 00:17:01,170
Come to think of it, I
guess I did smell gasoline.

252
00:17:01,253 --> 00:17:02,429
It's coming from us.

253
00:17:02,553 --> 00:17:04,671
Our bodies smell like a gas station.

254
00:17:08,793 --> 00:17:09,950
That's what it was shooting.

255
00:17:10,033 --> 00:17:10,863
Gasoline.

256
00:17:11,133 --> 00:17:14,370
It was shooting small amounts of
it at high speed, like bullets.

257
00:17:14,453 --> 00:17:15,283
Double.

258
00:17:15,366 --> 00:17:16,573
This is nuts!

259
00:17:16,893 --> 00:17:18,710
So he wasn't trying to wound us.

260
00:17:18,793 --> 00:17:20,510
He was dousing our bodies with gasoline.

261
00:17:20,593 --> 00:17:22,240
We're covered in this stuff.

262
00:17:24,153 --> 00:17:27,873
Looks like you finally caught
on, but it's too late now.

263
00:17:28,313 --> 00:17:30,313
Now all you need is a little jolt.

264
00:17:37,193 --> 00:17:38,023
Jotarou! Ah!

265
00:17:40,093 --> 00:17:40,923
Ah!

266
00:17:42,633 --> 00:17:43,463
Ah!

267
00:17:43,753 --> 00:17:44,583
Ah!

268
00:17:44,666 --> 00:17:46,533
Jotaro! Mr. Joestar! Stay back!

269
00:17:46,793 --> 00:17:48,430
We're soaking with gasoline, too!

270
00:17:48,513 --> 00:17:50,053
It's too dangerous! Ah!

271
00:17:55,373 --> 00:17:56,203
Jotaro!

272
00:17:57,613 --> 00:17:58,893
I win!

273
00:17:59,173 --> 00:18:01,853
Your valiant hero finally bit the dust!

274
00:18:09,173 --> 00:18:10,453
Is that so?

275
00:18:10,713 --> 00:18:14,233
And who exactly would
replace me, Chotaro Cujo?

276
00:18:21,073 --> 00:18:22,293
Let me guess.

277
00:18:22,433 --> 00:18:24,609
You thought it'd be you, you roadhog.

278
00:18:25,693 --> 00:18:28,573
You burrowed into the
ground with star platinum.

279
00:18:28,873 --> 00:18:31,755
So the only thing that
burned up was your jacket.

280
00:18:32,273 --> 00:18:36,313
A little parting wisdom what
you said earlier about paths?

281
00:18:37,433 --> 00:18:40,830
Was dead wrong you see in life you have to

282
00:18:40,913 --> 00:18:43,850
forge your own path no
one can do it for you!

283
00:18:43,933 --> 00:18:45,815
So I'll offer you some guidance!

284
00:18:47,753 --> 00:18:50,613
But first you have to go
through a little pain.

285
00:19:12,173 --> 00:19:13,893
That is how it's done.

286
00:19:14,733 --> 00:19:16,733
See, you just paved your own path.

287
00:19:16,913 --> 00:19:18,854
Congrats on being a fast learner.

288
00:19:19,113 --> 00:19:20,353
Here ends the lesson.

289
00:19:27,633 --> 00:19:28,930
What an odd guy.

290
00:19:29,013 --> 00:19:33,573
His arms are the size of boulders
and yet everything else is so small.

291
00:19:34,093 --> 00:19:35,333
Talk about a bluff.

292
00:19:40,093 --> 00:19:40,923
Hello.

293
00:19:41,153 --> 00:19:42,213
Going somewhere?

294
00:19:44,813 --> 00:19:46,048
Please don't kill me!

295
00:19:46,193 --> 00:19:48,733
I'm just sinners for the money! Honest!

296
00:20:03,053 --> 00:20:04,641
Oh, would you look at that?

297
00:20:04,753 --> 00:20:08,870
I can't believe the stand was disguising
such a small car that entire time.

298
00:20:08,953 --> 00:20:13,894
Kind of reminds me of a fluffy little sheep
that just had all of its wool shorn off.

299
00:20:14,833 --> 00:20:17,053
What a pathetic hunk of junk.

300
00:20:29,813 --> 00:20:32,695
Well, then, let's take
his car across the border.

301
00:20:32,793 --> 00:20:34,773
Only fair since he smashed ours.

302
00:20:35,133 --> 00:20:36,490
It's pretty beat up, though.

303
00:20:36,573 --> 00:20:38,514
I wonder if it'll last that long.

304
00:20:39,473 --> 00:20:40,433
Help! Help!

305
00:20:41,353 --> 00:20:44,410
You're on the next flight to Hong
Kong once we find an airport.

306
00:20:44,493 --> 00:20:46,693
Oh, no! Why? Shut up!

307
00:20:46,993 --> 00:20:50,270
Don't you understand that you're
in the way, you little brat?

308
00:20:50,353 --> 00:20:53,473
Er, we might not make it that far.

309
00:21:08,113 --> 00:21:09,070
Seiko!

310
00:21:09,153 --> 00:21:10,350
Seiko! Seiko!

311
00:21:10,433 --> 00:21:11,650
Seiko! Seiko!

312
00:21:11,733 --> 00:21:14,150
Seiko! Seiko! Seiko! Seiko!

313
00:21:14,233 --> 00:21:15,253
Seiko!

314
00:21:15,933 --> 00:21:21,193
My seven assassins have all
been defeated, and so easily!

315
00:21:22,293 --> 00:21:26,093
How could they be crushed
like that? The shame!

316
00:21:26,513 --> 00:21:29,353
I cannot bear to face Lordeo.

317
00:21:31,133 --> 00:21:32,193
Damn you!

318
00:21:32,393 --> 00:21:33,610
Curse you, Polnareff!

319
00:21:33,693 --> 00:21:34,813
Curse Kakyoin!

320
00:21:35,013 --> 00:21:37,484
Curse Jotaro and his wretched grandfather!

321
00:21:41,153 --> 00:21:45,413
I, Inyama, shall be your
next and final opponent!

322
00:21:45,893 --> 00:21:50,233
I will fight with my very own
stand, the stand of justice!

323
00:22:08,033 --> 00:22:10,770
All the old paintings on the tomb?

324
00:22:10,853 --> 00:22:12,810
They do the sand dance, don't you know!

325
00:22:12,893 --> 00:22:15,050
If they move too quick, oh well!

326
00:22:15,133 --> 00:22:17,470
They're falling down like a domino.

327
00:22:17,553 --> 00:22:20,130
All the birds are men by the Nile!

328
00:22:20,213 --> 00:22:22,190
You got the money on a bet!

329
00:22:22,273 --> 00:22:23,790
Called crocodiles!

330
00:22:23,873 --> 00:22:24,703
Oh-eh-oh!

331
00:22:24,786 --> 00:22:26,750
Then I snap their teeth on your cigarette!

332
00:22:26,833 --> 00:22:28,970
Falling tight to the hookah! I say!

333
00:22:29,053 --> 00:22:30,150
Oh-eh-oh!

334
00:22:30,233 --> 00:22:31,430
Oh-eh-oh!

335
00:22:31,513 --> 00:22:36,030
Oh-eh-oh!

336
00:22:36,113 --> 00:22:37,973
Walk like an Egyptian!

337
00:22:50,213 --> 00:22:52,750
The blonde waitresses take their trays!

338
00:22:52,833 --> 00:22:54,750
Spin around and they cross the floor!

339
00:22:54,833 --> 00:22:56,290
They've got the moves!

340
00:22:56,373 --> 00:22:59,430
You drop your drink,
then they bring you more!

341
00:22:59,513 --> 00:23:02,050
All the school kids so sick of books!

342
00:23:02,133 --> 00:23:04,130
They're like the punk and the metal band!

343
00:23:04,213 --> 00:23:05,673
When the buzzer rings!

344
00:23:06,453 --> 00:23:08,370
They're walking like an Egyptian!

345
00:23:08,453 --> 00:23:11,030
All the kids in the marketplace say!

346
00:23:11,113 --> 00:23:11,950
Walk

347
00:23:12,033 --> 00:23:19,033
like

348
00:23:19,173 --> 00:23:20,003
an Egyptian!

349
00:23:22,873 --> 00:23:24,610
The fog looks thicker up ahead!

350
00:23:24,693 --> 00:23:26,430
He's dead with that look of fear!

351
00:23:26,513 --> 00:23:28,490
What is with the people in this town?

352
00:23:28,573 --> 00:23:30,190
This is no ordinary murder!

353
00:23:30,273 --> 00:23:32,410
The Joestar party is on the third floor!

354
00:23:32,493 --> 00:23:33,323
Well hello!

355
00:23:33,406 --> 00:23:34,350
I see you are traveling!

356
00:23:34,433 --> 00:23:37,253
Ah salaam alaykum!
